On Saturday, the 10th of April, I started another random character, 
and this time the RNG made me a chaotic human priest.
I don't think I have ever finished the Priest quest before.
But last night I ascended this one.

On dungeon level 3, my cat brought me a wand from a shop, I engraved with
it, and it turned out to be a wand of WISHING! I know many people say an
early wand of wishing is a bad omen, but I decided to make the most of it.
Since I hadn't ascended a priest before, in any version of the game,
I wasn't particularly trying to keep conducts.. and soon after identifying
the wand and getting the traditional scrolls of charging, I decided to 
use another wish for a gray dragon scale mail. (As a priest I wanted to
keep wearing my robe, so I thought it was better to have that than a silver
one.)

On the Sokoban top level my concentration broke for a moment and I killed
a nymph with a wand of striking, breaking the mirror. Well, so I just had
to be more careful than usual until the bad luck would time out.
The prize was the bag this time.

The minetown altar was co-aligned, so I spent quite long there sacrificing.
I had to empty MANY wands and a bag of tricks, but finally Huhetotl gave
me Stormbringer which became my main weapon for the rest of the game.
Until that, the only thing I had wielded was my original mace, which was
already rusty (or was it very rusty.. I don't remember).
Later I got Trollsbane from the same altar, but never wielded it.
But when Huhetotl had given me Orcrist as the third artifact on another 
altar at dungeon level 10, I always switched to it when I went back to
Minetown to buy more protection, and also on the Home 1 level.

I must admit, I accidentally angered some peaceful creatures with Stormy
every now and then, and had to kill them.

On dungeon level 12, a throne gave me a genocide, and I decided to use
it to get rid of master mind flayers before seeing any of them.
Genoless was another conduct I was willing to lose in this game.
After a few more #sittings the same throne gave me a wish that I used
for an amulet of reflection, since I didn't have any source of reflection
yet and already had GDSM.
..and some #sittings later, I got ANOTHER GENOCIDE. 
Ok, I didn't want to see any regular mind flayers either.
That was a good throne, two genocides and a wish!

The quest was not that hard. On the locate level there were lots of 
undead monsters, but I stayed on the stairs as long as they kept 
coming, and every now and then climbed one level up, taking a few 
of them there and slaughtered them there, able to heal before more of
them came to bash me.

Somewhere in Gehennom I found a spellbook of identify, and it felt like
pure luxury when I finally got it to 0% failure rate.. Also, the spell
of remove curse at 0% failrate was nice when some monsters used the curse
attack.

In the Orcus town, a master lich surrounded me with the summon nasties
spell. When I was at about 50 Hp, I broke a wand of teleport to make
some room to get away from the crowd to heal.. and when I came back for
the L, ANOTHER summon nasties spell nearly killed me again.
Blah. My genoless and wishless conducts were already broken, so I gave
up: after breaking another wand of teleport to move the bad guys away,
I wished for a blessed scroll of genocide (hadn't seen any yet) and 
used it for L.

When I began fighting Orcus himself, he summoned Yeenoghu. But they were
both cowards who just hit and teleport, and finally escaped upstairs.
And from there, they escaped another level upstairs.
That's it. When I followed them to the next level, two above Orcus's
home level, I dug my bag of holding and took out.. a ring of teleport
control and a scroll of teleportation. I put the ring in my finger
and a blindfold around my head, and waited until the other staircase was
unoccupied, read the scroll and teleported there. Hmm, that was probably
the only scroll of teleport I used in this game. Well, anyway, once I
got myself to the stairs, Orcus and Yeenoghu were soon finished.

On the Sanctum level, the undead folks in the graveyard room seemed
to be awake. OK, I put a ring of conflict in my finger and let the
rest of them fight each other when I was bashing the nearest ones.
I kept conflict to speed my way around the temple as well. Again, I
had to check all four walls before finding the entrance. Maybe I should
once go the OTHER way around the temple..

Well, I went in, killed the high priest and the demon inside, grabbed
the amulet, and started making my way up.
The mysterious force was very friendly with me (I was chaotic, after all),
it only interfered with me four times: 42->43,43->44,41->41,34->35.

The Wizard didn't bother me much, either: the first time he re-appeared
was on dungeon level 16, and the next time was the guaranteed appearance
on the Earth level. And that was it.

The portal from Earth to Air was only about a dozen squares North from
the entrance, and about five squares West. I only used one wand of 
digging to get there, and even that didn't get empty.
On Air, I got swallowed by air elementals a few times and they once or
twice managed to get my Hp to around 60-70 before I broke out.
Fire and Water didn't cause any trouble or take too much time.

I arrived to Astral about halfway between the doors to the middle and
East branches. I checked that Death was at the East branch, Famine in
the middle and Pestilence at West.
I decided to try the middle altar first. Two or three zaps from a wand
of teleport to the angels and priests sped my way up, and the insects
didn't let Famine immediately to me. And when I saw there was only one
empty square between Famine and me, I used a wand of death and Famine
bothered me no more.
And guess what: the altar WAS the right one, Huhetotl's own high altar.

The first time I ascended a priest.
